name: Setup loop-engine
description: >
  GitHub Actions is a plain shell process, outside the Claude Code plugin-cache mechanism entirely
  (plugin bin/ PATH registration and installed-path lookup assume a live Claude Code session). This
  action fills loop-engine@paul-loop and ship-flow@paul-loop in via a pinned-tag `git clone` and
  exports LOOP_ENGINE_PATH/SHIP_FLOW_PATH, so `plugin-path.mjs` (loop-engine's own bundled resolver,
  BAC-753) resolves them the same way it would a local env-var override. Any job that runs a verify
  command, a loop-engine bin script, or this repo's own selftest should call this action first.

  The two plugins can be pinned to different tags (they version independently) — a shared clone
  would make one implicitly depend on the other's version, so they're cloned separately. Bump the
  tags below deliberately when you want a newer plugin version — this is an explicit semver pin, not
  a SHA channel that auto-follows (see paul-loop's ADR-0078 addendum for why).

  The clone URL is the CANONICAL repository path, not a GitHub redirect. It used to name the old
  namespace the repo was transferred away from. That works only for as long as GitHub's redirect
  holds, and a redirect stops the moment anyone creates a repository at the old path — at which
  point every consuming repo's CI clones and executes whatever is there. A stale namespace in a
  clone URL is a supply-chain hand-off waiting to happen, and nothing in a consuming repo's diff
  would show it changing hands.
runs:
  using: composite
  steps:
    - shell: bash
      run: |
        set -euo pipefail
        setup_dir=$(mktemp -d "${RUNNER_TEMP:-${TMPDIR:-/tmp}}/paul-loop.XXXXXXXX")
        # Keep successful clones for later steps; on failure remove only this invocation's directory.
        trap 'rm -rf "$setup_dir"' ERR
        git clone --depth 1 --branch loop-engine--{{LOOP_ENGINE_TAG}} \
          https://github.com/reach0908/paul-loop.git "$setup_dir/engine"
        git clone --depth 1 --branch ship-flow--{{SHIP_FLOW_TAG}} \
          https://github.com/reach0908/paul-loop.git "$setup_dir/ship"
        # Validate the actual artifacts before exporting executable paths to subsequent steps.
        LOOP_RUNTIME=shell LOOP_ENGINE_PATH="$setup_dir/engine/tools/loop-engine" \
          node "$setup_dir/engine/tools/loop-engine/bin/plugin-path.mjs" resolve loop-engine
        LOOP_RUNTIME=shell SHIP_FLOW_PATH="$setup_dir/ship/tools/ship-flow" \
          node "$setup_dir/engine/tools/loop-engine/bin/plugin-path.mjs" resolve ship-flow
        echo "LOOP_RUNTIME=shell" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
        echo "LOOP_ENGINE_PATH=$setup_dir/engine/tools/loop-engine" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
        echo "SHIP_FLOW_PATH=$setup_dir/ship/tools/ship-flow" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
